@@ -0,0 +1,397 @@
+title: CloudBQ pass 2 — L2 likelihood tiers, three execution surfaces, one gold table
+verdict: |
+  Verdict (pre-flight, 2026-10-16, no surface has yet run against wisekeybq): the second classification layer bins every open deal of
+  every pipeline by the certainty the pipeline actually records — IcAlps_OppoCertainty for Icalps (99.9 % filled), the stage probability
+  everywhere else — into Tier1 (≥ 0.9), Tier2 (≥ 0.75), Tier3 (≥ 0.5) and Tier4 (below), closed deals labelled Closed_won / Closed_lost.
+  Three surfaces compute it: N, a Vertex AI Workbench notebook (the lab: snapshot through the function's HubSpot client, numpy.digitize,
+  calibration from stage-entry dates, per-deal proof that RANGE_BUCKET agrees); Q, BigQuery-native (deal_tiers_v1 views over the daily
+  HubSpot → BigQuery sync, a scheduled MERGE into deal_tiers + deal_tiers_history); W, a deal.propertyChange webhook into the Cloud Run
+  function for one deal at a time. The arithmetic, the labels and the source resolution are the same between N and Q in evidence (one
+  constants file; step 7 proves RANGE_BUCKET ≡ digitize per deal) and read Conditional only until W is written; source, trigger, freshness,
+  identity and the idempotency mechanism diverge; the gold table and the StackSync write-back are the convergence point. Facts that constrain the
+  design: both certainty properties are fractions (0–1); SealSQ's stage probabilities are 0.1 / 0.2 / 0.5 / 1.0, so Tier2 is reachable
+  there only through a manual probability edit; Icalps overwrites certainty to 1.0 on closed-won, so calibration cannot use the snapshot
+  value; the warehouse holds no synced deals yet (the DTS transfer of scenario C is the prerequisite of Q).
+legend: |
+  Legend: Parity column colours — green Parallel, yellow Conditional, orange Divergent. Layers M0–M14 are the pass-2 layers (prefix M to
+  keep them apart from pass 1's L0–L17); Pipeline steps are the pass-2 sequence in order (constants → adapter columns → sync → apply → lab
+  snapshot → bins → parity → gold MERGE → equality → property → StackSync → schedule); Remediation rows T01– record what the CRM evidence
+  of 2026-10-16 corrected. Source: branch claude/cloud-run-bigquery-pipeline-e94ziy at 2026-10-16; CRM hub 9201667 via the HubSpot connector.
+surfaces:
+  N: N · Vertex AI Workbench notebook notebooks/l2_deal_tiers.ipynb (lab — HubSpot API snapshot, numpy.digitize, calibration, deal_tiers_lab)
+  Q: Q · BigQuery-native (sql/deal_tiers_v1.sql views + sql/deal_tiers_apply.sql scheduled MERGE over the daily HubSpot → BigQuery transfer)
+  W: W · Webhook CDC (HubSpot deal.propertyChange on dealstage / icalps_oppocertainty → Cloud Run function event path → MERGE one deal)
+motions:
+  - motion: N · Workbench notebook (lab)
+    acquire: git clone the branch on the instance; open notebooks/l2_deal_tiers.ipynb; constants from scoring/deal_tiers_v1.constants.json
+    ubuntu: 'Python 3 kernel: main.HubSpot (the function''s client) fetches every deal with the certainty candidates and hs_v2_date_entered_<stage>; pandas + numpy.digitize bin; google-cloud-bigquery loads deal_tiers_lab and runs RANGE_BUCKET on it'
+    driver: the operator runs the cells; no schedule
+    state: '`deal_tiers_lab` (truncated per run); nothing in HubSpot'
+    assessment: 'Fastest to iterate (minutes, orthogonal to Cloud Shell); the only surface that calibrates; a snapshot, not a feed — its result is evidence for Q, never the operational tier'
+  - motion: Q · BigQuery scheduled MERGE (production)
+    acquire: sql/apply.sh applies deals_synced_v1 (+ icalps_oppocertainty, is_closed, is_closed_won) → deal_certainty_v1 → deal_tiers_v1 → deal_tiers / deal_tiers_history / deal_tiers_summary_v1
+    ubuntu: 'bq: a scheduled query running sql/deal_tiers_apply.sql daily after the 02:00 UTC transfer; RANGE_BUCKET; MERGE on deal_id with IS DISTINCT FROM so unchanged deals write nothing'
+    driver: 'BigQuery scheduled query (UTC), after the DTS HubSpot transfer; manual: bq query < rendered script'
+    state: 'deal_tiers (gold, one row per deal, previous_tier, first/last change), deal_tiers_history (per change), deal_tiers_lab untouched'
+    assessment: 'Cheapest steady state (2,000 rows, pennies); freshness bounded by the transfer (≤ 26 h); blocked until the transfer exists (sql/sync_transfer.sh) and its table name is in .env'
+  - motion: W · Webhook CDC (event)
+    acquire: 'a HubSpot developer app with deal.creation and deal.propertyChange subscriptions (constants.watch_properties: dealstage, hs_deal_stage_probability, icalps_oppocertainty) → a dedicated route accepting HubSpot''s JSON array of events (not the function''s objectId event path) → GET the deal → MERGE one deal into deal_tiers'
+    ubuntu: 'Cloud Run function: validate the X-HubSpot-Signature, read the deal, resolve certainty by pipeline, RANGE_BUCKET-equivalent in Python (same constants), MERGE; HubSpot retries failed deliveries'
+    driver: HubSpot webhook (seconds after the edit); a public HTTPS endpoint — the private service needs a relay or an unauthenticated route with signature validation
+    state: deal_tiers / deal_tiers_history rows for the changed deal only; orchestrator = cloud-run-webhook
+    assessment: 'Near-real-time, but the one surface that needs a public endpoint, a developer app and signature validation; justified only if the tier must change within minutes of the edit — the daily Q lane covers the weekly reporting cadence'
+layers:
+  - id: M0
+    layer: Code acquisition & surface
+    N: notebooks/l2_deal_tiers.ipynb on a Workbench instance in wisekeybq (notebooks/README.md); constants read from the clone
+    Q: sql/deal_tiers_v1.sql + sql/deal_tiers_apply.sql via sql/apply.sh and a scheduled query (sql/scheduled_query.sh pattern)
+    W: cloud_function_new_deals/main.py event path extended for propertyChange (proposed, not written)
+    parity: Divergent
+    diverges: Three artefacts (notebook, SQL, Python function) from one constants file.
+    remediation: scoring/deal_tiers_v1.constants.json is the single source of edges, labels, sources; tests/test_deal_tiers.py keeps the SQL equal to it; the notebook reads it.
+    verified: tests/test_deal_tiers.py (edges/labels in SQL == constants; bisect reference == digitize semantics); notebook compiles (tests/test_notebook.py)
+  - id: M1
+    layer: Identity
+    N: 'the kernel''s ADC (instance SA or the operator after gcloud auth login --update-adc): BigQuery jobUser + dataEditor on the dataset, secretAccessor on hubspot-token'
+    Q: 'scheduled-query SA new-deals-sql@: jobUser, dataEditor on the dataset, dataViewer on the sync dataset (sql/scheduled_query.sh grants)'
+    W: 'the function SA new-deals-fn@ (dataEditor already granted by deploy.sh tables)'
+    parity: Divergent
+    diverges: Three principals; the same dataset-level grants.
+    remediation: Same DCL GRANT on the dataset for every identity (deploy.sh tables, scheduled_query.sh).
+    verified: grants read in deploy.sh / scheduled_query.sh; not yet applied — first authenticated run
+  - id: M2
+    layer: Source of certainty
+    N: 'HubSpot search API snapshot (≤ 10,000 results; ~2,000 deals): icalps_oppocertainty, hs_deal_stage_probability, hs_is_closed(_won), hs_v2_date_entered_<stage>'
+    Q: 'deals_synced_v1 over the DTS HubSpot transfer (full refresh daily 02:00 UTC) — icalps_oppocertainty, is_closed, is_closed_won added to the adapter view'
+    W: the webhook payload (objectId, propertyName, propertyValue) then GET /crm/v3/objects/deals/{id} for the rest
+    parity: Divergent
+    diverges: Same CRM, three transports; the sync is up to 26 h behind the API, the webhook is seconds behind.
+    remediation: deal_tiers_summary_v1 (Q) vs the lab summary (N) vs a CRM count per tier (query_crm_data) — differences must be explained by creation/edit timestamps after the sync.
+    verified: 'CRM facts of 2026-10-16: 799/800 Icalps deals carry icalps_oppocertainty; icalps_dealcertainty is a string with no values; win_probability mirrors the stage probability; hs_forecast_probability empty'
+  - id: M3
+    layer: Trigger & cadence
+    N: manual (Run All)
+    Q: scheduled query daily after the transfer (e.g. 03:00 UTC); manual bq query
+    W: deal.propertyChange on dealstage (SealSQ users move stages) and icalps_oppocertainty (Icalps users type certainty), plus hs_deal_stage_probability for manual edits
+    parity: Divergent
+    diverges: Operator / daily / event.
+    remediation: The gold table carries computed_at and orchestrator so a row says which lane wrote it and when.
+    verified: not yet — first authenticated run
+  - id: M4
+    layer: Certainty resolution per pipeline
+    N: 'certainty_source = icalps_oppocertainty for 766126206, hs_deal_stage_probability otherwise (constants certainty_source)'
+    Q: the same CASE in deal_certainty_v1
+    W: the same mapping in Python from the constants (not written yet)
+    parity: Conditional
+    diverges: Parallel for N and Q today; W is proposed, so its parity holds only once it is written from the constants and covered by tests/test_deal_tiers.py.
+    remediation: One constants file; the test asserts the SQL; W must import the same file.
+    verified: the CASE text is asserted by tests/test_deal_tiers.py; the notebook builds the column from the same constants
+  - id: M5
+    layer: Binning arithmetic
+    N: numpy.digitize(certainty, [0.5, 0.75, 0.9]) (right=False)
+    Q: RANGE_BUCKET(certainty, [0.5, 0.75, 0.9])
+    W: bisect.bisect_right(edges, certainty) (the pure-Python form the test uses; W not written yet)
+    parity: Conditional
+    diverges: N and Q are proven equal per deal (notebook §5); W inherits the parity only once written against the same constants.
+    remediation: ''
+    verified: 'tests/test_deal_tiers.py reference cases (0.49 → 0, 0.5 → 1, 0.75 → 2, 0.9 → 3, 1.0 → 3, None → None); notebook section 5 asserts RANGE_BUCKET == digitize per deal on the lab table (first authenticated run pending)'
+  - id: M6
+    layer: Labels and closed deals
+    N: Tier4_pipeline / Tier3 / Tier2 / Tier1 by bin_index; Closed_won / Closed_lost override; NULL certainty → no tier
+    Q: the same CASE in deal_tiers_v1 (array literal indexed by RANGE_BUCKET)
+    W: the same from the constants (not written yet)
+    parity: Conditional
+    diverges: N and Q share the labels and the closed override; an unknown closed state (NULL flag) is never tiered in Q; W pending.
+    remediation: ''
+    verified: tests/test_deal_tiers.py (labels array order, closed labels, NULL branches present in the SQL)
+  - id: M7
+    layer: Gold write
+    N: deal_tiers_lab (WRITE_TRUNCATE on every run) — never deal_tiers
+    Q: MERGE deal_tiers on deal_id keyed on @run_time; IS DISTINCT FROM on tier/certainty → previous_tier, last_changed_at; unchanged rows touch computed_at only; WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE retires deals gone from the sync (tier NULL, retired_at); 36 h freshness and half-rows guards
+    W: the same MERGE for one deal (orchestrator = cloud-run-webhook)
+    parity: Conditional
+    diverges: N writes a separate table; Q and W write the same gold table with the same MERGE semantics.
+    remediation: Equality check "lab vs gold" per pipeline × tier; differences must be deals edited after the sync.
+    verified: MERGE read (tests/test_deal_tiers.py asserts key, IS DISTINCT FROM, v_ variables); not yet executed
+  - id: M8
+    layer: History / audit
+    N: none (a snapshot)
+    Q: deal_tiers_history — one row per deal whose tier or certainty changed in the run (WHERE last_changed_at = v_run_ts)
+    W: the same table, one row per webhook-driven change
+    parity: Divergent
+    diverges: The lab keeps no history.
+    remediation: Accepted — the lab is evidence; the history belongs to the production lanes.
+    verified: DDL + INSERT … SELECT read; not yet executed
+  - id: M9
+    layer: Write-back to the CRM (deal_tier_v1)
+    N: 'prints the property definition (enumeration) and the StackSync mapping sheet rows (match key deal_id ↔ Record ID; tier → deal_tier_v1)'
+    Q: StackSync sync BigQuery → HubSpot from deal_tiers (one-way, scheduled or real-time per StackSync plan) after the property exists
+    W: could PATCH the deal directly (needs a write-scoped app) — not planned; StackSync stays the one writer
+    parity: Conditional
+    diverges: Only after `deal_tier_v1` exists in the portal (StackSync never creates definitions — mir-load hs-props pattern) and the sync is mapped.
+    remediation: One writer to the CRM (StackSync from deal_tiers); the function never writes the tier.
+    verified: open — property not created, StackSync not configured
+  - id: M10
+    layer: Calibration & statistics
+    N: 'fill rates per pipeline, value distributions, and per stage: deals that entered the stage (hs_v2_date_entered_<id>), won / lost / open, won share of closed vs the stage probability'
